# Docker / Pi Rules

- Restore PIM576 SPI/controller/backlight state before text writes and new display sessions' first valid frames, retaining the existing hardware handle. Preserve prepared session state across valid lease renewals and subsequent animation frames; do not reopen GPIO or periodically reset an active animation. The driver is pinned to ST7789 1.0.1; its `begin()` is a no-op, so recovery uses the verified initialization path. See ADR 0019.

- Custom Python runs only through the opt-in `edge-studio-script-helper` under the dedicated `edge-studio-code` account. Fixed installer/terminal setup enables it (`ENABLE_CUSTOM_CODE`); do not add generic root-agent HTTP code/package endpoints. Preserve user source `/opt/edge-studio-scripts` and jobs/data `/var/lib/edge-studio-scripts` on update/uninstall. Dependencies are manually installed per script, never during workflow runs. LCD frame sessions remain in the display helper, with no new backend device mounts. Keep SDK/helper/example runtime allowlists synchronized and use installer refresh for first adoption. This is trusted installed code, not a sandbox or deferred Module Builder runtime.

- PIM576 text output uses the opt-in display-helper service (`ENABLE_DISPLAYS=true`), bound to the configured Docker gateway with a backend-only token; never mount SPI/GPIO into the backend for display output. Preserve `.venv-display-helper`, its token and port across installer refreshes. First adoption on an older host agent requires an installer refresh to install the new helper file; later signed artifacts include it in their fixed allowlist.

- UI is exposed on HTTPS at `${FRONTEND_PORT:-8080}` (container port 443) with a self-signed cert in `${DATA_DIR:-./data}/certs`.
- SPI OS prerequisite setup is a separate explicit admin Hardware support action, like I2C setup: fixed apt-get Python prerequisites and raspi-config SPI enablement, with manual fallback and a reported reboot requirement. Ordinary display Enable/Repair must not silently run OS setup or reboot the host.
- Backend is internal behind frontend `/api` proxy.
- SQLite data lives in `${DATA_DIR:-./data}` mounted to `/data`.
- Minima data lives in `${MINIMA_DATA_DIR:-./minima}`.
- Host files are mounted read-only to `/host-files`.
- Docker socket is mounted read-only for prototype status only; treat it as sensitive.
- The root-owned host agent is installed by `install.sh` and exposes only token-protected, allowlisted hardware capability actions to the backend; never add generic shell, package, file, or service-management endpoints.
- GPIO input requires explicit `/dev/gpiochip0` device access and `gpiomon`; keep it optional, input-only, and documented as host hardware access.
- Raspberry Pi Camera capture uses the opt-in host-side Python camera helper (`ENABLE_CAMERA=true`) instead of camera CLI commands inside the backend container; keep it token-protected, reachable only from the configured Docker subnet where possible, and document privacy impact.
- BME280/BME680 and BH1750 sensor reads use the opt-in host-side Python sensor helper (`ENABLE_SENSORS=true`) instead of mounting `/dev/i2c-*` into the backend container; keep it token-protected, narrow, and documented as host I2C hardware access. Enable/repair installs smbus2 for BH1750 in the existing managed helper virtualenv.
- The optional local MQTT broker uses the `mqtt` Compose profile and exposes `${MQTT_PUBLIC_PORT:-1883}` only when explicitly enabled.
- The Edge Studio Compose network uses a configured subnet/gateway so containers have a stable route to host helpers after reboot/redeploy.
- `${UPDATE_AGENT_STATE_DIR:-./update-agent-state}` is mounted read-write into `update-agent` at `/state` and read-only into `backend` at `/update-agent-state` — the backend reads `last-applied-manifest.json` from it as the single source of truth for the app version reported in feedback submissions (see the Update Agent rules), never writes to it.
- Every long-running Compose service uses the shared `x-logging` anchor (`json-file`, `max-size: "10m"`, `max-file: "3"`); mirror it in `scripts/release/build-docker-compose.mjs`, and keep `createBodyFromInspect()` in `update-agent` applying the same fixed policy even to legacy containers. Existing installs need a verified installer rerun to migrate services not recreated by image-only updates. Match normalized webhook paths case-insensitively in nginx access-log masking and routing; the webhook location logs errors at `crit` only. See `docs/adr/0022-bound-external-automation-effects.md`.
